       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in hyponatremia:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " hypervolemic w HF: an ACEi plus a loop diuretic can correct refractory hyponatremia; if fluid restriction fails: escalating loop diuretic doses, sometimes w IV 0.9% saline; replace K and other lytes lost in the urine; SIADH: a loop diuretic may be combined w IV 0.9% saline."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Interactions (all diuretics):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " lithium—⍉, diuretics cut its clearance and risk toxicity; NSAIDs can blunt the diuretic and antiHTN effect of loop, K-sparing and thiazide diuretics."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
